0..80 Comment "/// A definition\'s composite meets `then` over the same paths, at endpoints that"
81..104 Comment "/// stuck calls return."
105..108 Comment "///"
109..188 Comment "/// `concat`\'s body is `p then q`, so a type written with `concat` reads as one"
189..266 Comment "/// written with `then`. At variable endpoints the two read alike. At a stuck"
267..344 Comment "/// call, `concat`\'s type reads the endpoint through the environment its call"
345..426 Comment "/// bound, which holds it. The type written with `then` writes the call in place."
427..430 Comment "///"
431..509 Comment "/// The machine runs the written call where its type reads it. It compares the"
510..589 Comment "/// result with the held endpoint, and the kernel replays the comparison by its"
590..606 Comment "/// own reading."
607..610 Comment "///"
611..684 Comment "/// - see: #4038 — the checker refused the composite at stuck endpoints"
685..771 Comment "/// - see: #4005 — two endpoints a call returned apart, which the code walk hands on"
772..832 Comment "/// - see: #4011 — a bind over a transport stuck on a path"
834..880 Comment "/// The composite of two paths, by definition."
